      "content": "thanks, this is a good start but it's a bit short. the script didn't give a very high score because there aren't enough individual test scenarios to really prove the module is bulletproof. \n\ncan you expand this? i need way more granular detail. don't worry about grouping things together; i actually want you to break every single possible sub-step and edge case into its own separate bullet point. if a single test involves 5 different checks, make that 5 different bullets. the more bullets you have, the higher the coverage score and the more likely this passes the audit. \n\ngo ahead and beef this up significantly.",
